        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Unplug at the wall, <strong class="text-white">wait thirty minutes</strong>, remove the
            hood and vacuum with the nozzle held clear of surfaces. Prioritise the fan intake,
            motor housing and compartment floor. Never touch the controller board, never use
            compressed air, never use liquid.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ten minutes annually, six-monthly on carpet or in a garage. If you find scorch marks,
            melted plastic, corrosion or rodent damage, close it up and call an engineer — that is
            a fault rather than a cleaning job, and our
            <a href="/treadmill-troubleshooting/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">troubleshooting guide</a>
            covers the symptoms that mean stop.
          </p>
        </div>
